Jesus' family lineage.
This is a record in the family tree of Jesus Christ. He is born of David. And he is born of Abraham as well.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah was the father of Perez and Zerah. Tamar was their mother. Perez was the father of Hezron. Hezron was the father of Ram.
Ram was the father of Amminadab. And Amminadab was the father of Nahshon. And Nahshon was the father of Salmon.
Salmon was the father of Boaz. Rahab was the mother of Boaz. Boaz was the father of Obed. Ruth was the mother of Obed. Obed was the father of Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. And David was the father of Solomon. And Solomon's mother was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon was the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam was the father of Abijah. Abijah was the father of Asa.
He was the father of Jehoshaphat, the father of Joram, the father of Ahaziah.
Uzziah is the father of Jotham. Jotham is the father of Ahaz. Ahaz is the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the son of Manasseh. Manasseh was the son of Amon. Amon was the son of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jeconiah and his brothers. At that time, the Jewish people were forced to leave for Babylon.
From this, the family line continued. Jechoniah was the father of Shealtiel. Shealtiel was the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was nothing to Abiud. Abiud was nothing to Eliacim. Eliacim was nothing to Azor.
Azor was nothing and they added. They added was nothing active. Active was nothing Eliud.
Eliud was the father of Elnathan. Elnathan was the father of Manaen. Manaen was the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus, who is called the Christ.
So, there were 14 generations from Abraham to David. And there were 14 from David until the Jewish people had to leave for Babylon. And there were 14 from that time to Christ, the birth of Jesus Christ.
This is how the birth of Jesus Christ happened. His mother Mary and Joseph were engaged and promised to marry. But before they started living together, it became clear to me that she was pregnant. She became pregnant by the power of the Holy Spirit.
Her husband, Youssef, was a good man. He didn't want to put her in an embarrassing situation in front of people. Therefore, he thought of divorcing her in secret.
While Joseph was contemplating this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream. The angel said, "Joseph, son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary as your wife. For the child conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
If God were to have a son, you would have to name him Jesus, because he would save his people from their sins.
All this happened so that what God said would happen. The prophet said it.
The virgin births a male child. A male child is born. And they name him Emmanuel. Emmanuel means "God is with us".
Joseph got up from his sleep. He did what the angel commanded him from his Lord. He took Mary into his house as his wife.
He did not have love with her until she gave birth to a son. And Joseph named him Jesus.
The Visit of the Wise Men to Jesus
Jesus is born in Bethlehem of Judea. This was at the time when Herod was king of Judea. After the birth of Jesus, magi came from the east to Jerusalem.
They said, "Where is the child who has been born to be the king of the Jews? For we observed his star when it rose, and we have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard this, he was deeply disturbed, and all the people of Jerusalem were also disturbed.
Herod called together all the chief priests of the people. He also called in the teachers of the law and asked them, "Where is the Messiah to be born?"
"In Bethlehem of Judea," they answered him. "For thus it is written by the prophet: 'And you, Bethlehem, in the land of Judah, are not the least among the rulers of Judah; for out of you will come a ruler who will shepherd my people Israel.'"
"But you, Bethlehem, though you are small among the clans of Judah, yet out of you shall come one who will be a ruler of my people Israel."
Then Herod secretly summoned the wise men. He asked them when the star had appeared exactly.
He sent them to Bethlehem. He said, "Go! Search diligently for the child. Do not seize him, but report to me about him as soon as possible. So that I too may go and worship him."
When the wise men did not heed the king's command, they continued on their way. The star that they had seen when they were in the East, went before them. Finally it stopped above the place where the child was.
As soon as they saw the star, they were very happy.
The wise men went to the house. There they saw the child with his mother Mary. They bowed down and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasures. They gave him gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
But God warned them in a dream not to return to Herod. They returned to their country by another way. Jesus' family flees to Egypt.
So, the wise men departed, and Joseph dreamed. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him. The angel said, "Arise!" "Take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt. Stay there until I tell you to return. Herod is going to look for the child. He wants to kill him."
Yosef got up. At night, he left for Egypt with the child and his mother Maryam.
Stay there until King Herod dies. In this way, the promise made by the Lord through the prophet will be fulfilled. He said, "I have surely loved you with an everlasting love; therefore with loving-kindness I will gather you." (Hosea 11:1)
Herod felt that the wise men had deceived him. He became very angry. He gave orders regarding Bethlehem and the surrounding areas. All the children who were two years old or less were to be killed. This was to coincide with the time that the wise men had seen the star.
In this way, the word of the prophet Ezekiel was fulfilled. For he had said,
Sounds are heard in Ramah. They are sounds of weeping and deep sorrow. Rachel weeps for her children. She refuses to be comforted, because they are gone. (Jeremiah 31:15) The return of Jesus' family to Nazareth.
When King Herod died, Joseph, who was still in Egypt, had a dream. In the dream, an angel of the Lord appeared to him.
The angel said, "Rise! Take the child and his mother. Return to the land of Israel. The people who were trying to kill the child are dead."
So Joseph rose up and took the child and his mother Mary to the land of Israel.
When Joseph heard that Archelaus had become king of Judea, in place of his father Herod, this caused Joseph such concern that he decided not to go there. Being warned in a dream, Joseph went instead to the region of Galilee.
