Jesus is deceived.
The Holy Spirit led Jesus into the wilderness. There the devil tempted him.
After forty days and forty nights of not eating, Jesus felt hungry.
The devil came to him. He said, "If you are the Son of God, tell these stones to become bread."
Jesus answered and said, "It is written, 'Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds from the mouth of God.'" (Deuteronomy 8:3)
Then the devil took Jesus to the holy city. And he made him stand on the highest point of the temple.
"If you are the Son of God," he said, "throw yourself down. For it is written, 'He will command his angels concerning you, to guard you closely. They will carry you in their arms, so that you will not strike your foot against a stone.'" (Psalm 91:11, 12)
Jesus answered and said to him, "It is written again, 'You shall not tempt the Lord your God.'" (Deuteronomy 6:16)
Finally, the devil took Jesus to a very high mountain. He showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory.
